save_HTTK_SHAPE

    _definition.id                HTTK_SHAPE
    _definition.scope             Category
    _definition.class             Loop
    _definition.update            2026-11-14
    _description.text
;
    The shapes of atom sites: per listed site, the arrangement of the bonds
    of the _geom_bond_ loop around it. A site carries at most one shape,
    over all of its bonds; a site that is not listed has no assigned shape.
    The loop is meaningful only together with a _geom_bond_ loop.
;
    _name.category_id             CIF_HTTK_HEAD
    _name.object_id               HTTK_SHAPE

    loop_
      _category_key.name
         '_httk_shape.atom_site_label'

save_

save_httk_shape.atom_site_label

    _definition.id                '_httk_shape.atom_site_label'
    _alias.definition_id          '_httk_shape_atom_site_label'
    _definition.update            2026-11-14
    _description.text
;
    The label of the atom site the shape belongs to. It must match one
    _atom_site.label of the block. For a site whose occupation is split over
    several _atom_site_ rows at one position, any one of those labels.
;
    _name.category_id             httk_shape
    _name.object_id               atom_site_label
    _type.purpose                 Link
    _type.source                  Related
    _type.container               Single
    _type.contents                Code
    _name.linked_item_id          '_atom_site.label'

save_

save_httk_shape.symbol

    _definition.id                '_httk_shape.symbol'
    _alias.definition_id          '_httk_shape_symbol'
    _definition.update            2026-11-14
    _description.text
;
    The shape of the bonds around the site: an IUPAC polyhedral symbol
    without its hyphen where IUPAC defines one (OC6 for OC-6, the
    octahedron), a label of the SHAPE program otherwise, or I for an
    irregular arrangement. The number in a named symbol is the number of
    atoms bonded to the site, counted over the bonds of the _geom_bond_ loop
    and their symmetry equivalents. I carries no number: its count is that
    number of bonds of the site, which must be at least three; httk reads it
    as I<n> with n that count, and also accepts I<n> written with the
    matching n.
;
    _name.category_id             httk_shape
    _name.object_id               symbol
    _type.purpose                 State
    _type.source                  Assigned
    _type.container               Single
    _type.contents                Code

    loop_
      _enumeration_set.state
         L2
         A2
         TP3
         TPY3
         TS3
         T4
         SP4
         SPY4
         SS4
         TBPY5
         SPY5
         OC6
         TPR6
         PBPY7
         OCF7
         TPRS7
         CU8
         SAPR8
         DD8
         HBPY8
         OCT8
         TPRT8
         TPRS8
         TPRS9
         HBPY9
         PPY6
         COC12
         ACOC12
         IC12
         I

save_

